From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Budik OS <info@budikstore.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:38:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] keyguard: make Graphene's second factor safe under the
 scene container

Dual Shade needs the scene container, which replaces the legacy keyguard
bouncer views with the Compose bouncer. GrapheneOS's fingerprint second
factor (fingerprint + extra PIN) only has UI in the legacy bouncer and
guarded the scene container path with unconditional throws, so SystemUI
crashed on boot with scene_container + dual_shade enabled.

- KeyguardSecurityContainerController: drop the "Compose bouncer support
  has not been added to Graphene's MFA!" throw.
- StatusBarKeyguardViewManager#showPrimaryBouncer: when the bouncer is
  already showing under the scene container there is nothing to
  re-request (upstream behaviour), instead of throwing.
- KeyguardUpdateMonitor: with the scene container, do not listen for
  keyguard fingerprint when the second factor is enabled. The user unlocks
  with the primary credential (PIN/password/pattern) in the Compose
  bouncer; fingerprint alone never unlocks (that path was already ignored
  by DeviceEntryFingerprintAuthRepository), so this is not a downgrade.
- KeyguardSecurityModel: never report BiometricSecondFactorPin under the
  scene container, so the Compose bouncer only sees primary modes.

Without the scene container nothing changes.
